@baseUrl = http://localhost:4002
@token = replace-with-bearer-token
@mediaId = replace-with-media-id

### Request a short-lived direct object-storage upload URL for an image or video
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scope": "Message",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "sizeBytes": 1024
}

### Confirm the direct PUT after uploading the exact declared bytes to ticket.uploadUrl
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{mediaId}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 400: unsupported content type
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scope": "Message",
  "contentType": "application/pdf",
  "sizeBytes": 1024
}

### 400: videos are message attachments only
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scope": "User",
  "contentType": "video/mp4",
  "sizeBytes": 1024
}

### Read a ready object (returns a direct storage URL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{mediaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete an object (uploader or administrator)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{mediaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Fetch a public image (anonymous; 302 to a signed storage URL). This is the durable src of a profile photo.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{mediaId}}/content

### A Message object is never reachable here, even for a participant
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{messageMediaId}}/content

### Upload the bytes through the API instead of the presigned storage URL (what a browser does)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{mediaId}}/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./probe.jpg

### 422: the body must match the content type and size the ticket was issued for
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{mediaId}}/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: image/png

< ./probe.jpg

### Upload a public content image for a blog cover (retain mediaObjectId and ticket.url)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"scope":"Content","contentType":"image/png","sizeBytes":1024}
